# {{ ft.name }}

A LoRA adapter for [{{ base_model.name }}](https://huggingface.co/{{ base_model.name }}) that turns a free-text request into one JSON function call: an intent, and a list of slots whose values are copied from the request. It was trained on the English (`{{ dataset.locale }}`) part of {{ dataset.name }} {{ dataset.version }}, which has {{ dataset.n_intents }} intents and {{ dataset.n_slot_types }} slot types.

```
"wake me up at nine am on friday"
  -> {"intent": "alarm_set", "slots": [{"type": "time", "value": "nine am"}, {"type": "date", "value": "friday"}]}
```

The adapter only works together with its base model. It is not a general chat model. It was compared with API models in the finetune-vs-api repository, whose `docs/method.md` defines every metric below.

