## Limitations

- English only: the training and the evaluation use the `{{ dataset.locale }}` part of {{ dataset.name }}. Other languages, other domains and spoken input were not tested.
- The labels are fixed: {{ dataset.n_intents }} intents and {{ dataset.n_slot_types }} slot types. A request outside them still gets one of them.
- Slot values are meant to be copied from the request, but a model can emit a value that is not in it{% if ft_facts %}; the share of predicted slot values missing from the request is in `results/comparison.json`{% endif %}. Nothing constrains the decoding by default, so the output can fail to follow the JSON format; the schema-valid rate is reported next to the task metrics.
- {{ dataset.name }} has been public since {{ citations.massive_year }}, and an MTEB mirror of it redistributes the test text, so the base model may have seen the test items. The data also repeats: {{ dataset.n_test_text_in_train }} test items have text that also occurs in train, which the evaluation reports separately.
- The comparison covers one task, one run per system and subsets of the test split, so small differences are not resolved. `docs/method.md` has the details, including how throughput and cost were measured.

